# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` and then restores and builds from scratch, so a host build output in the context
# is pure cost — and worse than cost.
#
# ⚠️ Its absence was a real build failure, not an inefficiency. `bin/Debug/net8.0/Backups/` holds folders written
# by `PgDumpBackupService` during local runs, and Docker's sender cannot read them (« Access is denied »), so the
# whole image build aborted before a single layer. It also shipped 207 MB of host-built binaries into the context
# for a build that discards them.
#
# The `.local/` line is the load-bearing one for security: it holds the self-generated CA **private key**, and a
# container image is a distributable artifact.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/

# Certificates, signing material and the local key store — never in an image.
**/.local/
**/*.pfx
**/*.key

# Runtime state written beside the app during a local run.
#
# ⚠️ **Anchored to the API project, NOT `**/`.** A bare `**/Files/` also matches the *source* directory
# `ClinicManagement.Application/Features/Files/`, which silently removed a whole feature from the build context
# and produced three CS0234s about a namespace that plainly exists on disk. A dockerignore pattern is matched
# against every path segment, so a generic folder name needs a path in front of it.
ClinicManagement.API/Files/
ClinicManagement.API/logs/
ClinicManagement.API/Backups/
logs/
**/TestResults/

**/*.user
**/.DS_Store
